machine: BusyBox init started as /linuxrc is not a container

Moonraker decides it runs in a container when /proc/1/cgroup names
docker or lxc, or else when PID 1 (first word of /proc/1/sched) is not
"init" or "systemd". The AD5X's boot command line starts BusyBox init as
init=/linuxrc, so PID 1 is "linuxrc" on the 6.6 and 7.3 kernels (which
have /proc/1/sched), Moonraker reported virtualization lxc, and
/machine/reboot and /machine/shutdown (Fluidd's Reboot and Shutdown)
were refused with "Cannot reboot from within a lxc container". "linuxrc"
is now on the list of real init names.

Upstream: not submitted (AD5X open OS)

--- a/moonraker/components/machine.py
+++ b/moonraker/components/machine.py
@@ -652,7 +652,10 @@
                 try:
                     data = sched_file.read_text().strip()
                     proc_name = data.split('\n')[0].split()[0]
-                    if proc_name not in ["init", "systemd"]:
+                    # Kiln OS: BusyBox init started as init=/linuxrc
+                    # (the AD5X's boot command line) is PID 1 on the
+                    # printer itself, not a container
+                    if proc_name not in ["init", "systemd", "linuxrc"]:
                         self.inside_container = True
                         virt_type = "container"
                         virt_id = "lxc"
